sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Ammonia beccarii Turing wavelength at 31 µm, Holocene 0 Ma — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 of the 31.37 µm (3.137e-05 m) Schnakenberg wavelength on a Holocene (0 Ma) Ammonia beccarii test face. Closes pass-1 R1 and R2. The 500 µm bar is 127 px on the 720-wide plate (3.937 µm/px). The gray>0.08 bounding boxes average 769.7 µm and the gray>0.32 cores average 761.8 µm, so the rim is not the discrepancy: these six tests are larger than the caption's rounded ~600 µm. FFT wavelengths are 31.18 µm (96²), 32.46 µm (128²), and 32.88 µm (160²), all within 5% of λ_c and not forced to equal it. Dispersion monodromy r = 0.9999997. γ sweep r = 0.995. GIF 12 frames at 720×540, CV similarity 92.2. Chronoseries 1/1 still has no predecessor and no successor. Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 85.6, reproducibility 87.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a46634a7d52b65a84c884100329f1df74d7ae443; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 87. Output judged: docs/media/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at a46634a7d52b65a84c884100329f1df74d7ae443, image/png, 813963 B, 1344×1032 px, artifact_sha256 2f66f42e479d98dc781b1aa79e81a123c69b021af59729252835c28b110ba765 (sha256 2f66f42e479d98dc781b1aa79e81a123c69b021af59729252835c28b110ba765), spec_fingerprint 5c78fef63a2342ef4c8a82571c976eb61e437c0ace429ce768a5b9e0809b609e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5c78fef63a2342ef4c8a82571c976eb61e437c0ace429ce768a5b9e0809b609e; artifact_sha256: 2f66f42e479d98dc781b1aa79e81a123c69b021af59729252835c28b110ba765; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/Ammonia_beccarii_Hillewaert_2012.jpg=c15a90be96e2b088..., datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6a6a4fb506092514..., datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=5ac93aba84d88754..., datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=12dc86d6408aac7a...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Hillewaert 2012 caption diameter ~600 µm, drawn 500 µm scale bar, CC BY-SA 4.0 plate | Subba & Ghosh 2023 pore diameter 0.564 µm and pore density 0.155 µm⁻² for Ammonia cf. beccarii | Petersen et al. 2016 pore frame of 562 µm² | Hayward et al. 2004 and Schönfeld et al. 2021 limits on the name A. beccarii; reconstructed_in_script: γ chosen so linear λ_c = 31.37 µm | Dv = 10.4 µm²/τ narrow band | Nonlinear field, γ sweep, equal-diffusion control, γ = 0 ablation | Two masks on the plate (gray>0.08 and gray>0.32) and FFT wavelengths on 96², 128², and 160² grids; transfer_boundary: Pigment-stripe / ocellus cohort language is transferred onto calcite pustule spacing | AFM pore numbers are Ammonia cf. beccarii, not the photographed North Sea individuals | 31.37 µm is the Delphi detail-scale assignment, not a spacing tabulated for this species; does_not_claim: That Ammonia beccarii has pigment ocelli | That 31.37 µm equals the pore diameter | That the caption's ~600 µm equals the bar-calibrated size of these six tests | That a predecessor or successor chronospecies exists in this 1/1 series | That the species-gallery Caryophyllia file is Ammonia | That a second assessor or a Lean kernel check was performed." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': \"Closed. Halo boxes average 769.7 µm and gray>0.32 cores average 761.8 µm on the 500 µm bar. The caption's ~600 µm is a round number, not the size of these six tests.\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed. FFT wavelengths are 31.18 µm (96²), 32.46 µm (128²), and 32.88 µm (160²). All sit within 5% of 31.37 µm; the finer grids run slightly long and were not adjusted to match.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Still open. Only grok-4.7 scored this audit. A second provider was not available in this run, and no second score was invented.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Still open. Lean 4 is not installed in this environment, so Loop_3108 was not kernel-checked.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.862"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent pass; no second provider)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

